    "done_when": "Done when: (1) at the two §0 arms, the 282-cell build and the 2,132-node build, the point batch compiles once, in at most 60 s and 64 GB peak host memory on the H200, fresh process and cache disabled, with the CPU compile wall and peak host memory recorded at both arms (no CPU bound is set until a CPU pass profile exists; §0 measured the CPU cold compile at 7,044 s), and the builder reports the batch loop's wall per batch at both arms, so a bounded compile followed by an unbounded loop is visible; (2) the built jet rows match the base build at every node of the 282-cell arm, and at the 2,132-node arm on a fixed subset of 64 nodes spread over the grid, for which the base program is evaluated over those nodes alone in one bounded job (the full 2,132-node base build never published its rows). The base compile does not shrink with the node count, so that job carries the full cold compile, about 7,044 s and 381 GB: one sirius job at --mem=450G and --time=04:00:00, with the batch loop limited to the 64 nodes: values bit-identical, and derivative entries within 1e-9 relative as the tangent-representation ruling allows for a scan-form tangent (or bit-identical where an exact tangent is kept); (3) the 500-cell coarse-tie census test ( test_census_neighbour_proposals_keep_saddles_across_coarse_ties ) runs against an empty operand store under --mem=64G and passes on its own assertion inside its own 900 s timeout, compile and batch loop included. That test timed out at 900 s on main 0b5972bfd with the values entry warm (carrier-vertex-identity, job 1295249), so clause (3) is the binding measure.",
